Subject: Provide native Host-Frame-Sources for Preview, Playback and Export

Allow an embedding Launcher to supply live Video-Frames to native FilmCraft
through the existing MediaSource-Interface. Register an optional authenticated
Loopback-Reader, when FILMCRAFT_FRAMES_PORT and FILMCRAFT_FRAMES_TOKEN are set.
Opaque .fcframes Descriptors identify Sources without storing End-Points or
Credentials in Project-Files. The Host owns Source-Authorization, Persistence
and Reconstruction when reopening a saved Project.

The Reader requests Media-Descriptions and exact Media-Ticks, then receives
straight RGBA8-Pixels. Validate Dimensions, Timing and Payload-Sizes before
Allocation, bound Response-Headers and Request-Deadlines, and poll Cancellation
while reading. Retry explicit Host-Back-Pressure within the same Deadline.
Report Cancellation separately from Decode-Failures, so it does not mark a
healthy Source as unreadable. Preview, Thumbnails and Export share this Reader.

Extend coherent Playback-Scheduling to native .fcframes Sources. Let a pending
Picture finish before catching up to the Playback-Clock, avoiding Starvation,
when Host-Rendering takes longer than one Frame-Interval. Paused Seeks and
Exports retain Requests for the exact Time.

Include Regression-Coverage for Cancellation, Back-Pressure, exact Ticks,
malformed Responses and Playback-Scheduling with pending Frames.

